On 2007-11-14, 3cnf...@gmail.com <3cnf...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Lifestealer seems less effective than Cleaver to me.

Could be true, depending mostly on your skill and the weapons'
enchantments.

Lifestealer is a two-handed sword: d12 vs small, 3d6 vs large, plus
d2+d8 when it drains a level.
Cleaver does d8+d4 vs small, d6+d4 versus large, plus d6 for being
Cleaver.

Average damages:
small   large   average
12.5    16.5    14.5    Lifestealer vs most monsters
10.5    12.0    11.25   Cleaver
 6.5    10.5     8.5    Lifestealer vs demons/undead
                        (aka two-handed sword)

In terms of pure HP damage, Lifestealer wins by a ~3 point margin.
Your enchantment and skill may vary.
Of course, Stealer's going to be a fair bit less painful to drain-
resistant baddies, so Cleaver gains the upper hand there.

